The first sentences of http://dag.github.com/cll/20/ give an=20
explanation of that:

    The following paragraphs list all the selma'o of Lojban,=20
    with a brief explanation of what each one is about, and=20
    reference to the chapter number where each is explained=20
    more fully. As usual, all selma'o names are given in=20
    capital letters (with "h" serving as the capital of "'")=20
    and are the names of a representative cmavo, often the most=20
    important or the first in alphabetical order.

In short, the cmavo are divided in to cmavo _types_; these=20
types are named by capitalizing a chosen cmavo of that type. =20
The LE type includes: le, lo, le'e, lo'e, le'i, lo'i, lei, loi. =20
In _The_Complete_Lojban_Language_=20
( http://dag.github.com/cll/ ); when a cmavo is described, the=20
selma'o is given; eg, the very first part of=20
http://dag.github.com/cll/6/2/ . =20

The "ku"s are closing the "lo"s which are of selma'o "LE".

